 route biomass to detritus' is tested, yet the four assert_trace_delta calls only cover system:daily_plants and system:daily_algae. There is no assertion for system:daily_shrimp → detritus.fine_g. The aggregate conservation check (assert_conserved) would still pass even if shrimp death routing regressed, so this is a genuine coverage gap between documented intent and actual verification."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-73c7af43","decision":"reject","rationale":"Verified stale: moderate_planted.toml already has alkalinity_meq_per_l = 0.58 and bicarbonate_mg_per_l = 35.4 committed at HEAD. Git status and git diff confirm no uncommitted modifications to either moderate_planted.toml or medium_planted.toml. The amendment describes a problem that has already been resolved, so there is no outstanding defect to address."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0ed29c5d-549f-466f-8fd6-84c8e5c92602"}
